From 66d0c387f40b3d14bc35349e1e565151b78b55f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AOSP RK3576 Baseline <uhf-platform@localbuild>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:32:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] uhf: add AIDL surface, UhfManager/UhfSession API,
 UhfService, JNI transport scaffold
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Completes the Phase 1 vertical slice on top of the previously-committed
protocol codec and session arbiter:

Framework (android.hardware.uhf, all @SystemApi/@hide per SRS §5):
- IUhfService/IUhfTagCallback/IUhfStateCallback AIDL, scoped to Phase 1
  (§4.1-4.8: lifecycle, identity, region, power, antennas, polled
  inventory, streaming — tag memory/security/EAS/peripherals are later
  phases and need no change here when they land, per §5.3's design goal).
- UhfManager/UhfSession/TagCallback client API matching §4's code samples,
  with ServiceSpecificException -> UhfException translated once, centrally.
- Parcelables: UhfDeviceInfo, UhfReaderInfo, UhfTag, InventoryParams,
  StreamParams, StreamStats, plus UhfException's ERROR_* constants.
- Context.UHF_SERVICE, PackageManager.FEATURE_UHF_READER, two permissions
  (UHF_READ normal, UHF_CONFIGURE signature|privileged — UHF_WRITE/UHF_RAW
  deferred to the phases that implement what they gate), SystemServiceRegistry
  and SystemServer wiring (feature-gated; NFR-C-06 falls out of the standard
  ServiceNotFoundException path for free, verified by reading it).

Services (com.android.server.uhf):
- UhfService: Binder/permission plumbing and per-session bookkeeping
  (stream params, stream stats, UID ownership per NFR-S-03) around
  UhfSessionArbiter, which stays framework-independent on purpose — this
  class is the only place android.hardware.uhf.* Parcelables get
  translated to/from the wire-codec types, so the arbiter's 74 host tests
  keep working without a framework build.
- UhfSessionArbiter: added getReaderInfo() (0x21) and inventory() (0x01,
  routed through the same stop/apply/restart path as FR-STR-13) plus
  isAntennaCheckEnabled()/isTransportOpen(), with 9 new tests.
- UhfSerialTransport + JNI scaffold: NOT built or run — no framework build
  attempted, no reader attached to this environment. The pump loop reuses
  UhfProtocol.scan()/scanWithStallRecovery() directly rather than
  reimplementing frame handling, so what runs through it is the tested
  code; only the termios/JNI plumbing itself is unverified. Native lib
  registration (services/core/jni/onload.cpp, Android.bp) intentionally
  not touched — out of scope for this pass, flagged rather than guessed at.
- SettingsRegionStore: FR-LC-09's persistence via Settings.Global,
  independent of reading the region back from the reader.

device/rockchip/rk3576/rk3576_u and device/rockchip/common in separate
commits apply the SRS Rev B ueventd/product-scoping fix this series'
review found.

Manual cross-check performed in lieu of a compiler (none of this compiles
without a full framework build): every IUhfService.aidl method has a
matching BinderService override and a matching UhfManager/UhfSession call
site; every UhfSessionArbiter method UhfService calls exists with a
matching signature. One real gap caught this way and fixed:
UhfSessionArbiter had no isAntennaCheckEnabled() getter even though
UhfService called it — added, with a test.

74/74 host tests still pass (UhfProtocol + UhfSessionArbiter, unaffected
by anything in this commit since it depends on the arbiter, not the
reverse).

Not yet done: hardware/rockchip/uhf/ AIDL HAL (Phase 2, per SRS §3.2's
phased alternative this whole patch deliberately defers), sdk/uhf-sdk/,
cts/tests/uhf/, and any actual framework build attempt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
